---
/* L03 - a probability is a long-run frequency, and odds are the same
   information written differently. One writer: the figures workstream E. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L03.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a forecaster's board carrying a grid of blank cards, with a hand pinning one more card to it, beside a tall rain gauge tube on the sill of a window streaked with rain."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L03-fig-title L03-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L03-fig-title">A probability is a long-run frequency, not a promise</title>
      <desc id="L03-fig-desc">
        On the left, two horizontal tallies, each on a track running from zero to one hundred similar
        mornings. The first is labelled said 0.9 and its filled bar reaches ninety, with the caption
        ninety of one hundred rained. The second is labelled said 0.6 and its filled bar reaches
        sixty, with the caption sixty of one hundred rained. The bars fill in turn. A note below
        says the card says nothing about today's sky and that swapping the forecaster changes the
        cards, not the rain. On the right, a small table converts probabilities into odds: 0.50 to
        1 to 1, 0.75 to 3 to 1, 0.90 to 9 to 1 and 0.99 to 99 to 1, under the formula p over one
        minus p.
      </desc>

      <!-- the two tallies -->
      <text x="24" y="40" class="fig-head">one hundred similar mornings</text>

      <text x="24" y="76" class="fig-text">said 0.9</text>
      <rect x="96" y="64" width="264" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect
        class="fig-fill"
        style="--m-duration: 1.2s; --m-delay: 0.1s;"
        x="96" y="64" width="237.6" height="18"
        fill="var(--color-prussian)"
      />
      <text x="96" y="100" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">90 of 100 rained</text>

      <text x="24" y="136" class="fig-text">said 0.6</text>
      <rect x="96" y="124" width="264" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect
        class="fig-fill"
        style="--m-duration: 1.2s; --m-delay: 0.7s;"
        x="96" y="124" width="158.4" height="18"
        fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)"
      />
      <text x="96" y="160" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">60 of 100 rained</text>

      <!-- the scale both tallies sit on -->
      <line x1="96" y1="178" x2="360" y2="178" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="96" y1="174" x2="96" y2="182" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="360" y1="174" x2="360" y2="182" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="96" y="196" class="fig-num">0</text>
      <text x="360" y="196" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">100</text>
      <text x="228" y="196" class="fig-text fig-text--dim" text-anchor="middle">similar mornings</text>

      <!-- what the number is not -->
      <rect x="24" y="214" width="336" height="104" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="38" y="236" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">the card says nothing about today</text>
      <text x="38" y="256" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">not that 90% of today's sky is wet,</text>
      <text x="38" y="272" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">and not that today's card is 90% correct</text>
      <text x="38" y="294" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">swap the forecaster and the cards read</text>
      <text x="38" y="310" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">differently; the rain does not move</text>

      <!-- odds: the same number, another way -->
      <text x="416" y="40" class="fig-head">odds</text>
      <text x="416" y="62" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">p / (1 - p)</text>
      <text x="416" y="92" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">probability</text>
      <text x="608" y="92" class="fig-text fig-text--dim" text-anchor="end">odds</text>
      <line x1="416" y1="100" x2="608" y2="100" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="416" y="122" class="fig-num">0.50</text>
      <text x="608" y="122" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">1 : 1</text>
      <text x="416" y="152" class="fig-num">0.75</text>
      <text x="608" y="152" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">3 : 1</text>
      <text x="416" y="182" class="fig-num">0.90</text>
      <text x="608" y="182" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">9 : 1</text>
      <text x="416" y="212" class="fig-num">0.99</text>
      <text x="608" y="212" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">99 : 1</text>
      <text x="416" y="248" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">odds multiply when</text>
      <text x="416" y="264" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">evidence stacks,</text>
      <text x="416" y="280" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">probabilities do not</text>
      <text x="416" y="304" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">9 to 1 is what a person</text>
      <text x="416" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">means by very sure</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L03</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">A card that says 0.9 is a claim about a population of similar mornings - about ninety of a hundred of them rain - and the same information written as odds is nine to one.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fig-head {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-text--ink {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text--dim {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  /* the one idea of motion: the tally fills to the claimed frequency */
  @keyframes l03-fill {
    from {
      transform: scaleX(0);
    }
    to {
      transform: scaleX(1);
    }
  }

  .fig-fill {
    transform-box: view-box;
    transform-origin: 96px 0;
    animation: l03-fill var(--m-duration, 1.2s) ease-out both;
    animation-delay: var(--m-delay, 0s);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .fig-fill {
      animation: none !important;
      transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
